{"id": "EUVD-2026-96899", "enisaUuid": "86ed9177-5585-3131-81eb-392de413f0bd", "description": "Frappe HR (hrms) before 16.11.0, including all 14.x and 15.x releases through 15.64.3, contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the whitelisted expire_allocation method that allows authenticated users to expire any leave allocation. Attackers without HR roles can name another employee's Leave Allocation in a POST request to zero its allocated leaves and wipe that employee's remaining leave balance.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T12:19:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T11:53:06", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind03/frappe-hrms-expire-allocation-missing-authorization-20261010", "https://github.com/frappe/hrms/blob/0a54d2c7b8b6043e2705b6f557b6ed65260670dd/hrms/hr/doctype/leave_ledger_entry/leave_ledger_entry.py#L199-L228", "https://github.com/frappe/hrms/commit/6ab7a50347367413b78ad5bd5d9e4b8c6653c81f", "https://github.com/frappe/hrms/releases/tag/v16.11.0", "https://github.com/frappe/hrms", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/frappe-hr-hrms-before-16.11.0-missing-authorization-via-expire-allocation"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7xfq-498m-4hrf", "CVE-2026-108733"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "db457c5c-5761-36b1-b246-34f01a8ca686", "product": {"name": "hrms", "vendor": {"name": "frappe"}}, "product_version": "0 <16.11.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9b5f8c43-79dc-32b3-98b7-dee192f2e785", "vendor": {"name": "frappe"}}], "isExploited": false}